  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Version: 2021.4.2\nDescription of the bug: The first time a VRCStation is used, the user is teleported way above it, often out of world bounds. Other users see them disappear upon entering the station. Upon leaving the station, they will re-appear for others in the correct position. Any subsequent attempts to enter the station will work correctly.\nI've only seen this bug occuring with one of my avatars, which uses components to animate unguligrade legs, but otherwise is fairly mundane. (The rigging for animations and IK is set up to see a standard humanoid rig, with \"fake\" humanoid leg bones being controlled by VRChat, and the actual legs controlled by components.)\nReproduction steps: Load into the specific avatar that causes the issue, use a station. It reliably reproduces the first time a VRCStation is used on a world. Changing out of the avatar, then going back into it, will allow the bug to be repeatedly reproduced on the same station.\nAny extra files?: I've attached images to show what happens - they were taken on Desktop, but the issue also reproduces on PCVR too.",
